 and the critical final bit of information, explicitly calculating that N-2 queries leave exactly 1 bit of unresolved entropy, which the SxS winner omits entirely.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = brief mention, 3-4 = substantive section with clear reasoning, 5-6 = comprehensive analysis that adds significant depth', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit triangle inequality application', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly writes out the triangle inequality step ||P_{c_1} - P_{c_2}||_1 ≤ ||P_{c_1} - P'||_1 + ||P' - P_{c_2}||_1 to derive the contradiction, while the SxS winner states the inequality without explicit algebraic demonstration.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor difference, 3-4 = clearer demonstration of the key step, 5-6 = critical explicitness for proof verification', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'LaTeX formatting consistency', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro uses consistent LaTeX delimiters ($...$) throughout, while the SxS winner uses inconsistent notation mixing $\\cA$, $\\eps$, and raw text like '1/4' without delimiters in some places.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor inconsistency, 3-4 = noticeable difference in readability, 5-6 = substantially superior professional formatting', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Section headers for proof structure', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro uses explicit descriptive section headers ('Adversarial Strategy (REASONING)', 'Query Counting (NON-TECHNICAL)', 'Total Variation Bound (VERIFICATION)', 'Information-Theoretic Perspective') that clarify the proof's logical flow, while the SxS winner uses numbered sections with minimal description.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor organizational difference, 3-4 = clearer navigational structure, 5-6 = substantially superior pedagogical organization', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit contradiction derivation', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly derives the numerical contradiction comparing 4/3N > 2/100N with clear inequality statement, while the SxS winner states '2/(3N) > eps = 1/(100N)' more concisely without showing the combined bound.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor difference, 3-4 = clearer verification step, 5-6 = critical explicitness for proof completeness', 'rating': 3}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Explicit adversary strategy specification', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 provides a concrete, step-by-step adversarial answering rule with numbered conditions and invariant maintenance, while the SxS winner describes the adversary more abstractly without explicit algorithmic specification.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Query counting with repeat query analysis', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly distinguishes between distinct queries and repeat queries, proving that only t ≤ N-2 distinct queries matter and repeat queries reveal zero information, whereas the SxS winner does not analyze this distinction.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Information-theoretic perspective section', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 includes a dedicated section framing the lower bound in information-theoretic terms (bits revealed per query, residual uncertainty), which the SxS winner omits entirely.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit completion construction', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly constructs Completion 0 and Completion 1 with clear bullet-point formatting showing exactly how u and v are swapped, while the SxS winner describes completions more briefly without structured presentation.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'LaTeX spacing and display formatting', 'description': "GPT 5.2 uses superior LaTeX formatting including manual spacing adjustments [2mm] in cases, aligned equation environments with explicit tags (1), and clearer fraction display, compared to the SxS winner's more compact and less readable LaTeX.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Invariant formalization with tag', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly names and tags the adversary invariant as (Inv) with formal mathematical notation, while the SxS winner states constraints informally without formal invariant naming.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 24877, 'output_tokens': 4632, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.105338}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.105338}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 24877, 'output_tokens': 4632, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.105338}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.105338}}] 
