erpretation affecting proof structure, 5-6 = fundamental error invalidating the proof's premise", 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Kostant cohomology citation', 'description': "GPT 5.2 explicitly invokes Kostant's theorem on Lie algebra cohomology H^2(g_-,g) to establish vanishing in homogeneity 3 for n>2, providing the rigorous representation-theoretic foundation.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = mentions Kostant vaguely, 3-4 = clear statement of relevant cohomology, 5-6 = precise computation with specific homogeneity degrees', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Minimal homogeneity argument', 'description': "GPT 5.2 employs the standard parabolic geometry technique of working with minimal homogeneity component r, ensuring quadratic curvature terms don't contribute to the algebraic cocycle condition.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = implicit use, 3-4 = explicit mention, 5-6 = rigorous application with contradiction argument', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Bianchi identity precision', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 correctly states that at minimal homogeneity, the differential Bianchi identity reduces to the algebraic condition ∂κ^(r)=0 (not involving κ^(1) terms), matching standard parabolic geometry theory.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor imprecision, 3-4 = mostly correct, 5-6 = exactly matches textbook treatment', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Dimensional analysis completeness', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 provides both the cohomological explanation (H^2(g_-,g)^(3)≠0 for n=2) and the tensor translation via the divergence identity ∇_ℓ W_{ij}^{kℓ} = (n-2)C_{ij}^k for why n=2 is special.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = one explanation, 3-4 = two explanations with one incomplete, 5-6 = both rigorous and complementary', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Structural organization with explicit model identification', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 opens with explicit identification of G=SL(n+1,R) and P as line stabilizer, establishing the parabolic geometry framework before proceeding to curvature analysis.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = men