2026-03-25 07:32:59,343 494048 INFO ? odoo.addons.preference_ranking.models.models: eval_ab response: [{'task_id': 'tv_stem_16044', 'prompt': 'Let $a,b,c$ be positive real numbers. Prove that \n \n\\[ \\frac{a(a+c-2b)}{b} + \\frac{b(b+a-2c)}{c}+\\frac{c(c+b-2a)}{a} \\geq \\frac{a^3+b^3+c^3-3abc}{ab+bc+ca} \\]', 'evaluation_result': {'response_a': {'instruction_following': {'score': 6, 'reason': 'Complete checklist: [X] Prove the stated inequality for positive reals a,b,c. [X] Provide rigorous mathematical proof. [X] Handle the cyclic sum structure correctly. [X] Establish equality conditions. No unrequested content added. Format is appropriate mathematical proof style. All instruction elements satisfied with zero omissions.'}, 'truthfulness': {'score': 5, 'reason': "All mathematical claims verified: [VERIFIED] Identity a³+b³+c³-3abc = (a+b+c)(a²+b²+c²-ab-bc-ca) = p(p²-3q). [VERIFIED] Algebraic manipulation of cyclic sum to p(∑a/b)-3p. [VERIFIED] Cauchy-Schwarz application: (∑a/b)(∑ab) ≥ (∑a)² is correct. [VERIFIED] Equality condition a=b=c derived correctly. One minor issue: The Cauchy-Schwarz step uses (∑a/√b · √ab)² ≥ (∑a)², which is valid but slightly non-standard presentation—could be written more directly as (∑a/b)(∑ab) ≥ (∑a)² by Titu's lemma or weighted Cauchy. This is verifiable and correct, just slightly unusual formatting. No false claims."}, 'prompt_correctness': {'score': 6, 'reason': 'Correctness audit: [CORRECT] Left side transformation to p(∑a/b)-3p. [CORRECT] Right side transformation to p(p²-3q)/q. [CORRECT] Reduction to proving ∑a/b ≥ p²/q. [CORRECT] Proof of reduced inequality via Cauchy-Schwarz. [CORRECT] Equality condition analysis. The proof is complete, correct, and verifiable. All requirements of the inequality proof are satisfied.'}, 'writing_style': {'score': 5, 'reason': "Quality audit: Strengths: Clear structure with labeled 'Proof', systematic algebraic manipulation, logical flow. Minor issues identified: (1) The Cauchy-Schwarz presentation as (∑a/√b·√ab)² is slightly awkward—standard Titu's lemma or direct Cauchy would be cleaner. (2) 'Summation gives' could be more explicit about cyclic sum notation. (3) Final 'as required. ∎' is slightly informal. These are trivial style preferences; overall professional mathematical writing quality."}, 'verbosity': {'score': 5, 'reason': "Length analysis: Ideal length for this inequality proof is medium (establishing substitution, transforming both sides, applying known inequality, checking equality). Response achieves this: substitutions p,q introduced efficiently, each algebraic step shown without redundancy, Cauchy-Schwarz applied directly, conclusion concise. Nothing can be cut: each step is necessary for rigor. Nothing is missing: all transformations are explicit. Only trivial trimming possible: the final restatement of the original inequality is slightly redundant given the 'as required' clause, but this is standard proof convention."}, 'overall_quality': {'weighted_score': 5.45, 'reason': 'Weighted: IF×0.25 + Truth×0.25 + Correctness×0.20 + Writing×0.15 + Verbosity×0.15 = 5.45'}}, 'response_b': {'instruction_following': {'score': 5, 'reason': 'Checklist: [X] Prove the stated inequality. [X] Use appropriate mathematical techniques. [X] Establish equality conditions. [X] Handle positive real constraint. Minor issue: The substitution a=y+z, b=z+x, c=x+y is valid (any positive a,b,c can be so represented with x,y,z>0), but this is an unrequested approach not implied by the prompt. While mathematically valid, this adds a specific technique not required. No other instruction elements missed. Score capped at 5 due to unrequested methodological choice that shapes the entire proof structure.'}, 'truthfulness': {'score': 4, 'reason': "Fact-check: [VERIFIED] Homogeneity of degree 1: LHS each term is degree (1+1-1)=1, RHS is (3-3)/2=0... wait—rechecking: a³+b³+c³-3abc has degree 3, ab+bc+ca has degree 2, so RHS has degree 1. Correct. [VERIFIED] Substitution a=y+z et