2026-03-25 07:50:11,142 494048 INFO ? odoo.addons.preference_ranking.models.models: tasks1_response---------------------------[{'index': 0, 'prompt': 'You are given a setup and statement to prove or derive. Your job is to provide a complete and correct proof. Think carefully, trying multiple approaches if you are stuck, and finally give a cleaned up proof under the heading ## Proof. If you are unable to complete the proof, be honest and say so.\n\n## Setup\nLet $(\\rho, u)$ be a smooth solution to the Cauchy problem for the one-dimensional compressible Navier-Stokes equations on the interval $(x,t) \\in {\\mathbb R}\\times(0,T]$ for any $T>0$. The system of equations is given by:\n$$\n\\begin{cases}\n\\rho_t + (\\rho u)_x = 0 & \\text{(S1)} \\\\\n(\\rho u)_t + (\\rho u^2)_x + p_x = (\\mu(\\rho)u_x)_x & \\text{(S2)}\n\\end{cases}\n$$\nwhere $\\rho$ is the density, $u$ is the velocity, the pressure $p$ is given by $p(\\rho) = \\rho^\\gamma$ for a constant $\\gamma > 1$, and the viscosity $\\mu$ is given by $\\mu(\\rho) = 1 + \\rho^\\beta$ for a constant $\\beta \\ge 0$.\n\nThe initial conditions are:\n$$\n(\\rho(x,0), u(x,0)) = (\\rho_0(x), u_0(x)) \\quad \\text{for } x \\in {\\mathbb R} \\quad \\text{(S3)}\n$$\n\nWe assume the following standard energy estimate holds for the solution:\n**Lemma 4 (Energy Estimate)**\nLet $(\\rho,u)$ be a smooth solution to (S1)-(S3). Then for any $T>0$, it holds\n$$\n\\int_{{\\mathbb R}}(\\rho u^{2}+\\rho^{\\gamma})(t)dx+\\int_{0}^{T}\\int_{{\\mathbb R}}(1+\\rho^\\beta)(u_{x})^{2}dx\\leq C. \\quad \\text{(S4)}\n$$\nwhere $C$ is a constant depending on the initial data. This implies in particular that for any $t \\in [0, T]$, $\\|\\sqrt{\\rho}u(t)\\|_{L^2}$ and $\\|\\rho(t)\\|_{L^1}$ are bounded by a constant $C$.\n## Theorem\n**Lemma 5 (Uniform upper bound of the density)**\nSuppose that $(\\rho,u)$ is a smooth solution to the Cauchy problem (S1)-(S3). Then for any $T>0$, there exists an absolute constant $C>0$ which depends on the initial data and $\\beta\\ge 0$ such that\n$$\n\\rho(x,t)\\leq C, \\quad (x,t)\\in {\\mathbb R}\\times(0,T].\n$$', 'status': 'ACCEPT', 'result': {'status': 'ACCEPT', 'rejection_reason': None, 'justification': 'The prompt provides a complete mathematical setup with reference text (the compressible Navier-Stokes equations, initial conditions, energy estimate Lemma 4, and the theorem to prove as Lemma 5). This is a well-defined mathematical proof request with all necessary context provided. No rejection categories apply.'}, 'accepted': True, 'error': None, 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1034, 'output_tokens': 87, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003112}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003112}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1034, 'output_tokens': 87, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003112}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003112}}] 
