le': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minimal LaTeX, mostly inline, 3-4 = display math present, 5-6 = polished LaTeX with aligned equations and proper delimiters', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit Kraft inequality application', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro does not use the Kraft inequality explicitly in Direction 2, instead using a direct counting argument; the SxS winner uses Kraft inequality in part (i).', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = no counting argument, 3-4 = standard counting, 5-6 = this rubric is inapplicable as Gemini does not demonstrate superiority here', 'rating': 1}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Explicit lemma statements with proofs', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 states and proves explicit lemmas (Lemma 1, Lemma 2) with clear hypotheses and conclusions, whereas the SxS winner embeds these arguments inline without formal lemma structure.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1 = minor structural difference, 6 = dramatically clearer modular organization with fully proved lemmas', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Step-by-step strategy articulation before details', 'description': "GPT 5.2 provides explicit 'Strategy' subsections outlining the proof approach before diving into technical details, while the SxS winner proceeds directly to constructions without strategic overview.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1 = minimal strategic guidance, 6 = comprehensive strategic framing that aids comprehension', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit non-circularity justification', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 contains a dedicated subsection explicitly proving the oracle construction is non-circular, whereas the SxS winner assumes this without explicit verification.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1 = implicit handling, 6 = explicit rigorous justification of a critical logical requirement', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Concrete boundary case verification', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a complete 'Boundary Cases' section computing both sides of the equality for singletons and [0,1]^n, while the SxS winner provides no concrete examples.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1 = no examples, 6 = thorough verification with detailed calculations for multiple cases', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Explicit Kraft inequality application with bounds', 'description': "GPT 5.2 explicitly derives the bound (13) with constant c_1 and proves the prefix-free coding fact, while the SxS winner uses 'standard' pruning without explicit quantitative analysis.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1 = vague reference to standard results, 6 = complete quantitative derivation with explicit constants', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'LaTeX equation numbering and cross-referencing', 'description': "GPT 5.2 uses numbered equations (1)-(20) with explicit cross-references (e.g., 'by (3)', 'combine (15) and (17)'), while the SxS winner uses unnumbered displays with implicit references.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1 = unnumbered equations, 6 = systematic numbered equations enabling precise logical tracking', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit oracle encoding construction', 'description': "GPT 5.2 provides the explicit formula (14) defining A using a standard computable pairing function, while the SxS winner describes the oracle more informally as 'coding... the rational centre'.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1 = informal description, 6 = fully explicit computable construction', 'rating': 5}], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 38711, 'output_tokens': 4887, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.136066}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.136066}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 38711, 'output_tokens': 4887, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.136066}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.136066}}] 
