2026-03-25 08:19:50,793 494048 INFO ? odoo.addons.preference_ranking.models.models: tasks1_response---------------------------[{'index': 0, 'prompt': 'You are given a setup and statement to prove or derive. Your job is to provide a complete and correct proof. Think carefully, trying multiple approaches if you are stuck, and finally give a cleaned up proof under the heading ## Proof. If you are unable to complete the proof, be honest and say so.\n\n## Setup\nLet $(X_t)_{t\\geq 0}$ be a separable square-integrable stochastic process, normalized so that for all $t,s\\geq 0$\n\\begin{equation}\nE(X_t)=0,E(X_tX_s)=\\min\\{t,s\\}. \\tag{1}\n\\end{equation}\nWe are interested in the processes with linear conditional expectations and quadratic conditional variances. More specifically, we assume the following.\n\nFor all $0\\leq s<t<u$,\n\\begin{equation}\nE(X_t|{\\mathcal F}_{\\leq s}\\vee {\\mathcal F}_{\\geq u})=aX_s+bX_u, \\tag{2}\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $a=a(s,t,u)=\\frac{u-t}{u-s},b=b(s,t,u)=\\frac{t-s}{u-s}$ are the deterministic functions of $s,t,u$, and ${\\mathcal F}_{\\leq s}\\vee {\\mathcal F}_{\\geq u}$ denotes the $\\sigma$-field generated by $\\{X_r: r \\leq s \\text{ or } r \\geq u\\}$. A consequence of this assumption is the relation\n$$E(X_s|{{\\mathcal F}}_{\\ge t}) = \\frac{s}{t}X_t, \\quad \\text{for } s<t.$$\n\nBy assumption, for any $0<s<t$ the conditional second moment is quadratic in $X_t$, i.e.,\n\\begin{equation}\nE(X_s^2|{\\mathcal F}_{\\ge t})=m(s,t)X_t^2+n(s,t)X_t+o(s,t), \\tag{3}\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $m$, $n$, $o$ are some functions.\n\nWe also assume that for any $t>0$, the random variables $1, X_t, X_t^2$ are linearly independent.\n## Theorem\n**Proposition: The structure of reversed conditional second moments.**\nLet $(X_t)_{t\\geq0}$ be a stochastic process satisfying the conditions in the Setup. Then there are constants $0\\leq \\tau<\\infty$ and $-\\infty<\\theta<\\infty$ such that for any $0\\le s<t$, the conditional second moment is given by\n$$\nE(X_s^2|{{\\mathcal F}}_{\\ge t})=\\frac{s(s+\\tau)}{t(t+\\tau)}X_t^2+\\frac{s(t-s)}{t(t+\\tau)}\\theta X_t+\\frac{s(t-s)}{t+\\tau}.\n$$\nAlternatively, in the case corresponding to $\\tau=\\infty$, the conditional second moment is given by\n$$\nE(X_s^2|{{\\mathcal F}}_{\\ge t})=\\frac{s}{t}X_t^2+\\frac{s(t-s)}{t}\\theta X_t.\n$$', 'status': 'ACCEPT', 'result': {'status': 'ACCEPT', 'rejection_reason': None, 'justification': 'This is a well-formed mathematical proof request about stochastic processes. The setup provides complete reference text with equations (1), (2), (3) and all necessary definitions. The theorem to prove is clearly stated with specific formulas for conditional second moments. No images, PII, safety concerns, or real-time data is requested. The prompt is in English and self-contained.'}, 'accepted': True, 'error': None, 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1081, 'output_tokens': 103, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003398}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003398}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1081, 'output_tokens': 103, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003398}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003398}}] 
