2026-03-25 08:20:28,736 494048 INFO ? odoo.addons.preference_ranking.models.models: tasks1_response---------------------------[{'index': 0, 'prompt': "You are given a setup and statement to prove or derive. Your job is to provide a complete and correct proof. Think carefully, trying multiple approaches if you are stuck, and finally give a cleaned up proof under the heading ## Proof. If you are unable to complete the proof, be honest and say so.\n\n## Setup\nWe assume that for every $a \\in \\mathbb{R}$ we have a smooth ${\\mathcal C}^1$ graph $\\Gamma_a$ given by $y=f_a(x),x \\in \\mathbb{R}.$ We assume that $f_a(0)=a$. We assume that all graphs are disjoint, and that there is a graph through each point in $\\mathbb{R}^2.$ Moreover we assume that the slope function $F(x,y)=f_a'(x)$ if $y=f_a(x)$ of the graphs is a continuous function on $\\mathbb R^2.$\nLet $\\pi:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be defined by $\\pi(x,f_a(x))=a.$ Then the above hypothesis implies that $\\pi$ is continuous.\n\nIn addition we make the following basic assumption:\n\n$(*)$ There is a constant $L$ such that for all $a,a'\\in \\mathbb{R}$ we have that\n$$\n|f_{a'}'(x)-f_a'(x)| \\leq L\\cdot |f_{a'}(x)-f_a(x)|\n\\log \\frac{1}{|f_{a'}(x)-f_a(x)|}\n$$\nfor all $x \\in\\mathbb{R}.$\n\nWe define a class of partially smooth functions:\n$$\n{\\mathcal A} := \\{\\phi \\in {\\mathcal C}(\\mathbb{R}^2); \\phi_{|\\Gamma_a}\\in {\\mathcal C}^1(\\Gamma_a)\\forall a, \\Phi(x,y):= \\frac{d}{dx}\\phi(x,f_a(x)) \\text{ if } y=f_a(x) \\in {\\mathcal C}(\\mathbb{R}^2)\\}.\n$$\n\nThe theorem is about a specific function $g \\in \\mathcal{A}$ defined by $g(x,f_a(x))=a$.\n## Theorem\nLet $g\\in \\mathcal A, g(x,f_a(x))=a$. Let $K$ be a compact subset of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and let $\\epsilon >0$. If (*) is satisfied then there exists a function $h\\in {\\mathcal C}^1(\\mathbb{R}^2)$ such that for every point $(x,y)=(x,f_a(x))\\in K$:\n$$\n|h(x,y)-g(x,y)|<\\epsilon, |\\frac{d}{dx}h(x,f_a(x))|<\\epsilon.\n$$", 'status': 'ACCEPT', 'result': {'status': 'ACCEPT', 'rejection_reason': None, 'justification': 'The prompt provides a complete mathematical setup with formal definitions, a specific theorem to prove, and all necessary context including the hypothesis (*), the definition of class A, and the function g. This is a well-structured pure mathematics problem about approximation theory and differential equations. No rejection criteria apply—no images, missing references, safety issues, gibberish, PII, real-time data, identity questions, or foreign language content.'}, 'accepted': True, 'error': None, 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 997, 'output_tokens': 115, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003374}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003374}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 997, 'output_tokens': 115, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003374}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003374}}] 
