ose.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 minor difference, 3-4 clear pedagogical advantage, 5-6 critical step made dramatically clearer', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Surjectivity subsection demarcation', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro uses '*Surjectivity onto P̄:*' as an explicit subsection header, while the SxS winner uses only \\medskip\\noindent \\textbf{Surjectivity} with less visual distinction from the main text.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 minor formatting, 3-4 clearer sectioning, 5-6 substantially better structural signaling', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Explicit generation argument for surjectivity', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly states the generation argument: 'the splitting field P̄ is generated over Φ̄ entirely by the roots of the polynomials in Ω̄' and 'Since all of these generating roots already lie in σ(P)', whereas the SxS winner uses a more indirect argument via monomorphisms of normal extensions.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 minor difference, 3-4 clearer reasoning, 5-6 substantially more direct and transparent argument', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'LaTeX spacing in field notation', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro consistently uses proper LaTeX spacing with \\mathrm{P} and \\overline{\\mathrm{P}} for field notation, while the SxS winner uses raw P and \\overline P without roman font, creating visual inconsistency with standard mathematical typesetting conventions.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 minor typographical, 3-4 clear typesetting advantage, 5-6 professional vs amateur rendering', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Explicit contradiction structure signaling', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly marks the contradiction argument with 'Suppose, for the sake of contradiction' and 'This contradiction proves,' while the SxS winner uses 'If E_0 ≠ P' without explicit contradiction framing, making the logical structure less transparent.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 minor rhetorical difference, 3-4 clearer logical structure, 5-6 dramatically clearer proof methodology', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'E