n content, structure, and mathematical rigor. Both use Instruction Following (complete proof with clear steps), Truthfulness (correct application of Borsuk-Ulam/area arguments), Prompt Correctness (fully addresses the geometric problem), Writing Style (formal mathematical exposition with LaTeX), and Verbosity (appropriate detail with concrete example). The SxS winner and GPT 5.2 both establish: (1) rotation by 180° preserves area, (2) Γ must intersect its rotated image via contradiction using equal-area components, (3) intersection points yield antipodal points on Γ through O. Both include the same circle example with r=√(2/π) and closing offer for additional examples. No discernible difference in quality, correctness, or completeness.'}, 'rubrics_vs_gemini': [{'name': 'LaTeX delimiter consistency', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro uses consistent LaTeX delimiters ($...$) throughout the mathematical expressions, while the SxS winner mixes \\( ... \\) and bare text, creating formatting inconsistencies.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 minor inconsistency, 3-4 noticeable inconsistency, 5-6 severe inconsistency in the SxS winner', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit verification calculation in example', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro includes explicit algebraic verification showing that the selected points A and B are collinear with O through slope calculation, while the SxS winner only asserts collinearity without computational verification.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 minor difference, 3-4 clear difference, 5-6 substantial difference in rigor', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Non-symmetric example construction', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro constructs a concrete non-symmetric example (parabola y = x² - 1/3) that requires non-trivial analysis to verify the theorem, while the SxS winner uses a trivial symmetric example (circle centered at O) where any diameter works.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 minor difference, 3-4 clear pedagogical difference, 5-6 substantial difference in example quality', 