dary term power counting for S_KW', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly computes the scaling of √γ, ∂ₙ, and the boundary integrand √γ φ ∂ₙφ ~ z^(2Δ-D), showing why this cancels the leading divergence; the SxS winner presents the boundary term evaluation without showing this power-counting derivation.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Tangential gradient analysis for remaining convergence', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly identifies that after the boundary term cancellation, the remaining divergence comes from tangential derivatives ∂ᵢφ with scaling z^(2Δ-D+1), leading to the modified condition Δ > (D-2)/2; the SxS winner does not explain this mechanism.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Concrete numerical examples with specific parameters', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 provides two explicit numerical examples (D=3, m²L²=-2 inside window; D=3, m²L²=0 outside window) with computed values of ν, Δ±, and explicit normalizability checks; the SxS winner has no numerical illustrations.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Summary table organizing all cases', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 includes a structured table comparing S_usual vs S_KW across mass ranges, normalizable roots, and dimension bounds; the SxS winner has no such organizing visual structure.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit on-shell bulk term vanishing check', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly computes □z^Δ = Δ(Δ-D)z^Δ/L² and verifies (-□+m²)z^Δ = 0 on-shell for Δ=Δ±, showing the bulk integrand vanishes pointwise; the SxS winner asserts this without explicit demonstration.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better,