\log F_{q,\\nu}(\\rho)\n$$\n## Theorem\n**Theorem 2**\n\nSuppose $\\nu$ satisfies LSI with constant $\\alpha > 0$. Let $q > 1$. Along the Langevin dynamics, for all $t \\ge 0$,\n$$R_{q,\\nu}(\\rho_t) \\le e^{-\\frac{2\\alpha}{q}t} R_{q,\\nu}(\\rho_0)$$", 'status': 'ACCEPT', 'result': {'status': 'ACCEPT', 'rejection_reason': None, 'justification': "This is a mathematical proof problem asking to derive a theorem about R'enyi divergence convergence under Langevin dynamics. The prompt includes all necessary mathematical definitions, setup, and the statement to prove. No external references, images, real-time data, PII, safety concerns, or foreign language content is present."}, 'accepted': True, 'error': None, 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1075, 'output_tokens': 91, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003242}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003242}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1075, 'output_tokens': 91, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003242}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003242}}] 
