ndition into the integration step.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor notation difference, 3-4 = clear structural difference in method, 5-6 = fundamental methodological superiority', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit algebraic inversion step', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro includes the explicit step of inverting both sides to solve for u, showing the algebraic manipulation that yields the final formula.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor clarity difference, 3-4 = noticeable step present vs absent, 5-6 = critical derivation step clearly shown vs omitted', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Physical interpretation of blow-up singularity', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro provides concrete physical examples (chemical reactions, thermal runaway, combustion, population dynamics) and explains the singularity as marking model validity limits.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = slightly more detail, 3-4 = substantive additional context, 5-6 = dramatically richer physical interpretation', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'LaTeX formatting consistency', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro uses consistent LaTeX delimiters ($$ for display math) and proper spacing around operators, while the SxS winner mixes $$ and \\[...\\] with occasional formatting inconsistencies.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor formatting preference, 3-4 = clear consistency advantage, 5-6 = substantially cleaner mathematical typography', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Structured section hierarchy', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro uses clear hierarchical section headers (--- separators, bold headers) with explicit strategy declaration, while the SxS winner uses numbered lists without clear thematic breaks.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor organizational preference, 3-4 = clearer structural navigation, 5-6 = dramatically superior document architecture', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0