K}$ and $\\mathbf{K}'$ are the two Dirac nodes of the honeycomb lattice.\n\nThe ansatzes for the holon and spinon Green's functions are:\n$$\nG_B (\\vec{r}) = \\alpha_b \\frac{\\mathcal{P}_b}{r^{2 \\Delta_b}} \\\\\nG_F (\\vec{r}) = \\alpha_f \\frac{1}{r^{2 \\Delta_f + 1}} \\left( e^{- i \\mathbf{K} \\cdot \\mathbf{r}} \\bcancel{r} + e^{- i \\mathbf{K}' \\cdot \\mathbf{r}} \\cancel{r} \\right)\n$$\nHere, $\\Delta_b$ and $\\Delta_f$ are the critical scaling exponents for holons and spinons, respectively. $\\alpha_b$ and $\\alpha_f$ are constants. $\\mathcal{P}_b$ is a projection matrix in the sublattice basis. With no loss of generality, we set the phase offset between Dirac cones of c- and f-electrons to zero, such that\n$$\n\\mathcal{P}_b = \\frac{1}{2} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n$$\nThe condition for the conformally invariant fixed point is that the product of the Green's function and the self-energy is a constant matrix in momentum space. Specifically, considering the component near one of the Dirac points (denoted by subscript L):\n$$\nG_{fL}(\\vec{q}) \\Sigma_{fL} (\\vec{q}) = - \\mathbb{1}\n$$\n## Theorem\nAt the conformally invariant fixed point of the 2+1D multichannel Kondo lattice on a honeycomb lattice, described by the large-N self-consistent equations and the conformal ansatz for the Green's functions, the scaling exponents of the fermionic spinon ($\\Delta_f$) and bosonic holon ($\\Delta_b$) Green's functions satisfy the relation:\n$$\n\\Delta_f + \\Delta_b = 2.\n$$", 'evaluation_result': {'response_a': {'instruction_following': {'score': 5, 'reason': "The response follows the instruction to provide a complete proof under the heading '## Proof'. It uses a cleaned-up structure with numbered steps. I checked for: (1) heading requirement - satisfied with '## Proof'; (2) complete proof - provided; (3) multiple approaches - not explicitly shown but the proof is direct and complete; (4) honesty if stuck - not needed as proof succeeded. 