e the product G_f Σ_f, while SxS winner suppresses matrix structure into 'dimensionless function of direction'.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Complementary boson sector verification', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro includes a complete verification using the bosonic self-energy equation Σ_bL to independently confirm Δ_f + Δ_b = 2, demonstrating mutual consistency of both self-consistent equations.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit substitution verification', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro substitutes the derived constraint Δ_b = 2 - Δ_f back into the momentum-space product to explicitly verify the |q|^0 result, rather than only checking dimensional consistency.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Physical interpretation of constraint', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explains why only the sum is fixed (inverse scaling dimensions of operator and dual self-energy) and connects individual dimensions to 1/N corrections, while SxS winner only notes it's 'one linear equation'.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'LaTeX formatting quality', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro uses proper display math environments with consistent spacing and alignment, while SxS winner has occasional formatting issues (e.g., 'stated upfront' header formatting, inconsistent equation numbering).", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'o