ntly uses $$...$$ display math delimiters for important equations (kernel definition, extension definition, main limit formula), while the SxS winner mixes \\[...\\] with occasional inline formatting and has less consistent visual hierarchy for key formulas.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 if formatting is inconsistent, 3-4 if generally good, 5-6 if display math is strategically used for all major structural equations', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit mention of Leibniz rule for differentiation', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly cites the 'Leibniz rule' as the justification for passing derivatives under the integral sign in the interior regularity argument, while the SxS winner only appeals to 'dominated convergence' without naming the specific theorem for derivatives.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 if no justification given, 3-4 if dominated convergence mentioned, 5-6 if Leibniz rule is explicitly named', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 29761, 'output_tokens': 3696, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.103874}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.103874}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 29761, 'output_tokens': 3696, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.103874}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.103874}}] 
