ons, 5-6=numbered steps with descriptive headers guiding the reader', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Variable definition and notation introduction', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explicitly defines all elementary symmetric polynomials (e_1, e_2, e_3, e_4) with their meanings before use, while the SxS winner introduces notation (P, x_i) without explicit definition of the symmetric polynomial framework.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2=notation introduced implicitly, 3-4=some definitions given, 5-6=all notation explicitly defined with domain specifications', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Clear problem reduction strategy', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly states a reduction principle (linearity in cd) with labeled sections showing how the problem simplifies to checking endpoint cases, while the SxS winner jumps directly into substitution without explaining the strategic motivation.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = reduction mentioned briefly, 3-4 = clear reduction with some explanation, 5-6 = explicit principled reduction with full justification', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Structural organization with numbered sections', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 uses clearly labeled sections (## 1), ## 2), etc.) with descriptive headers that map the proof architecture, while the SxS winner uses informal \\medskip breaks and bold text without hierarchical structure.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = some visual breaks, 3-4 = clear sectioning, 5-6 = rigorous hierarchical organization with descriptive headers', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit equality case verification', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a dedicated 'Equality check' section that explicitly computes and verifies both the symmetric case (1,1,1,1) and the nontrivial case (0,4/3,4/3,4/3), while the SxS winner only mentions equality conditions in passing without explicit verification.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = equality cases mentioned, 3-4 = some cases verified, 5-6 = comprehensive explicit verification of all equality cases', 'ratin