rrect, is unnecessarily verbose with redundant explanations and a less streamlined argument. Gemini 3 Pro establishes the key identity (1) immediately via density of π(A₀)Ω, then cleanly handles the supremum over product states through faithful cyclic representations (Step 3), whereas GPT 5.2 belabors the same points across sections 2a-2c with excessive notational machinery. GPT 5.2's 'Check the special case n=1' section is entirely superfluous—the prompt asks to prove a general statement, not to verify a special case—and its universal representation argument in 2c, while correct, is less direct than Gemini's approach. Both proofs are mathematically sound, but Gemini's superior Information Density and more disciplined Instruction Following (no extraneous content) give it the edge."}, 'rubrics_vs_gemini': [{'name': 'LaTeX delimiter consistency', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro uses consistent LaTeX delimiters ($...$ for inline, $$...$$ for display) throughout the response, while the SxS winner uses a mix of TeX commands (\\textbf, \\medskip, \\noindent) with minimal LaTeX math formatting.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 minor inconsistency, 3-4 noticeable formatting differences, 5-6 substantially better LaTeX rendering', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit verification section', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro includes a dedicated 'Part 3: Verification for n=1' section that explicitly checks the edge case n=1, explaining how each structural component simplifies; the SxS winner only parenthetically mentions this without elaboration.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 brief mention, 3-4 structured but limited verification, 5-6 comprehensive edge case analysis with clear explanations', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Definition of auxiliary constructions', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explicitly defines the linear functional ω_S with its domain, positivity proof, and unitality verification; the SxS winner introduces equivalent concepts without explicit definition or proof of state properties.', 'sca