raint to exclude |N|=2 for O'N. Prompt Correctness: Both correctly prove that the only 1/3-quasirandom groups are J₁ and O'N. Writing Style: Both use identical clear mathematical exposition with proper LaTeX formatting. Verbosity: Both are equally concise and complete with matching 'Key Takeaways' sections. The responses appear to be word-for-word identical, suggesting either identical model outputs or the same underlying system."}, 'rubrics_vs_gemini': [{'name': 'LaTeX formatting quality', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro uses proper LaTeX delimiters ($...$) for mathematical expressions throughout, while the SxS winner uses inconsistent formatting (bare symbols like \\tfrac13 without delimiters in some places).', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 minor LaTeX issues, 3-4 noticeable improvement in rendering, 5-6 substantially better mathematical typography', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Structural organization with clear section headers', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro includes clearly demarcated section headers (## Prerequisites, ## Proof, ## Key Takeaways) that improve navigability, while the SxS winner lacks consistent visual separation between proof sections.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 minor formatting difference, 3-4 clear structural advantage, 5-6 dramatically superior organization', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Explicit contradiction structure in proof', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly frames the proof using 'Assume for contradiction' and clearly signals 'Since assuming G is not simple leads to contradictions in all possible cases, G must be simple,' making the logical structure transparent.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 slightly clearer, 3-4 noticeably more explicit logical structure, 5-6 substantially superior exposition of proof technique', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Numerical approximation for clarity', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro provides decimal approximations (≈ 1.0003, ≈ 2.84) that give readers immediate intuition about the bound tightness, which the SxS winner omits.', 'sc