scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = brief mention of definitions, 3-4 = clear dedicated section with multiple definitions, 5-6 = comprehensive formal definitions with standard results explicitly enumerated', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Proof structure with labeled steps', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro uses explicitly numbered steps ('Step 1', 'Step 2', 'Step 3') and a dedicated 'Verification of the Contradiction' subsection to organize the logical flow.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = some structural markers, 3-4 = clear numbered steps throughout, 5-6 = comprehensive hierarchical structure with thematic section breaks', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Concrete base construction with verification', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explicitly constructs the witness a = 1 + n/p and immediately verifies that gcd(a,n) = 1 before using it, showing the concrete calculation that any common divisor must divide 1.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = witness mentioned without full verification, 3-4 = explicit construction with coprimality verification, 5-6 = detailed step-by-step verification integrated into the logical flow', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Binomial expansion with term-by-term analysis', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro writes out the full binomial expansion of (1 + n/p)^(n-1) and explicitly analyzes which terms vanish modulo n by computing (n/p)^2 = n·q.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = binomial theorem mentioned, 3-4 = expansion written with some term analysis, 5-6 = complete expansion with explicit modular vanishing argument for j ≥ 2', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Final contradiction explicit arithmetic', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explicitly derives that requiring 1 - n/p ≡ 1 (mod n) forces n | n/p, hence 1 | 1/p, hence p | 1, making the impossibility transparent.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = contradiction stated, 3-4 = some steps shown, 5-6 = complete chain of implications ending with p | 1 explicitly written out', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'LaTeX formatting with display equations', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro