escription': "GPT 5.2 explicitly states 'This contradicts the defining property of a Carmichael number' before the conclusion, while the SxS winner ends with 'contradicting' embedded in the final step.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = contradiction implied; 3-4 = contradiction mentioned; 5-6 = explicit standalone contradiction statement that recaps what was violated', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Separate conclusion section', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a distinct 'Conclusion' section that restates the theorem in bold, while the SxS winner ends with 'Hence no p² divides n' without a dedicated concluding paragraph.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = theorem restated implicitly; 3-4 = brief concluding sentence; 5-6 = dedicated section with emphatic restatement of the result', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Clear statement of base choice rationale', 'description': "GPT 5.2 explicitly justifies why the chosen base a satisfies gcd(a,n)=1 with a dedicated verification sentence, while the SxS winner states '(a,n)=1' without explicit verification.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = base stated without justification; 3-4 = brief justification; 5-6 = explicit step-by-step verification of coprimality conditions', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Binomial expansion explicitly shown', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 displays the binomial expansion formula explicitly before modular reduction, while the SxS winner jumps directly to the congruence without showing the intermediate expansion.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = formula used without display; 3-4 = formula mentioned; 5-6 = explicit displayed formula with terms shown before reduction', 'rating': 4}], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 17045, 'output_tokens': 4610, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.08941}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.08941}, 'token_usage_cumulati