ction and EVT, while SxS winner uses standard radius-halving construction; Gemini's method demonstrates deeper structural understanding.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2=minor variation, 3-4=meaningfully different valid approach, 5-6=fundamentally distinct rigorous construction with clear advantages', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Post-proof analysis section', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro includes dedicated section analyzing where metric structure is essential and why theorem fails for non-metrizable spaces, while SxS winner ends abruptly after proof.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2=brief concluding remark, 3-4=substantial analysis of one aspect, 5-6=comprehensive analysis of both metric dependence and failure in general topological spaces', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Structural organization with clear stage divisions', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro uses explicit 'Stage 1/2/3' headers and 'Definitions and Preliminaries' section with visual separators, while SxS winner is single continuous prose block.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2=some paragraph breaks, 3-4=clear section headers, 5-6=explicit numbered stages with hierarchical organization and visual separators', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit justification for technique choice', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro includes 'Justification for our technique' subsection explaining motivation for distance-to-complement approach, while SxS winner presents technique without motivational explanation.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2=implicit motivation, 3-4=brief explicit justification, 5-6=dedicated subsection with clear reasoning for methodological choices', 'rating': 5}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Explicit definition section', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a clearly labeled section at the beginning titled with 'Chosen definitions' or similar that explicitly states all definitions used in the proof before proceeding.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 if definitions are scattered, 3-4 if present but less organized, 5-6 if dedicated, clearly labeled section with full definitions', 'ratin