tains its minimum on compact X and defines m := min_{x∈X} g(x), then uses m > 0 to define δ := m/2.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 if minimum existence implicit, 3-4 if mentioned, 5-6 if fully explicit with m definition and δ = m/2 construction', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Verification by contradiction', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 verifies δ is a Lebesgue number using an explicit proof by contradiction: assuming y ∉ U_i leads to f_i(x) < δ contradicting f_i(x) ≥ 2δ.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 if direct verification only, 3-4 if brief contradiction, 5-6 if explicit contradiction structure with clear inequality chain', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Section on metric-specific structure', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a dedicated section titled 'Where the metric structure was used' explicitly identifying the two crucial metric-dependent ingredients (distance functions and explicit radii).", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 if no such section, 3-4 if brief mention, 5-6 if dedicated section with numbered points and explicit contrast with general topology', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Section on failure for non-metrizable spaces', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 includes a section explaining why the theorem fails for compact Hausdorff non-metrizable spaces, with explicit examples ([0,ω_1] and βℕ).', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 if no generalization, 3-4 if brief mention, 5-6 if dedicated section with explicit examples and connection to uniform spaces', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'LaTeX display math for key definitions', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 uses proper LaTeX display math (\\[...\\] or $$...$$) for the formal definition of Lebesgue covering property and the equivalent diameter formulation.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 if inline only, 3-4 if some display, 5-6 if consistent display math for key definitions with proper formatting', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Structural organization with numbered stages', 'description': "GPT 5.2 uses explicit 'Stage 1', 'Stage 2', 'Stage 3' headings to organize the proof into logical phases (lemma construction, Lebe