2026-03-25 08:46:15,482 494048 INFO ? odoo.addons.preference_ranking.models.models: tasks1_response---------------------------[{'index': 0, 'prompt': 'You are given a setup and statement to prove or derive. Your job is to provide a complete and correct proof. Think carefully, trying multiple approaches if you are stuck, and finally give a cleaned up proof under the heading ## Proof. If you are unable to complete the proof, be honest and say so.\n\n## Setup\nLet $(X_t)_{t\\geq 0}$ be a separable square-integrable stochastic process, normalized so that for all $t,s\\geq 0$\n\\begin{equation}\nE(X_t)=0,E(X_tX_s)=\\min\\{t,s\\}. \\tag{1}\n\\end{equation}\nWe are interested in the processes with linear conditional expectations and quadratic conditional variances. More specifically, we assume the following.\n\nFor all $0\\leq s<t<u$,\n\\begin{equation}\nE(X_t|{\\mathcal F}_{\\leq s}\\vee {\\mathcal F}_{\\geq u})=aX_s+bX_u, \\tag{2}\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $a=a(s,t,u)=\\frac{u-t}{u-s},b=b(s,t,u)=\\frac{t-s}{u-s}$ are the deterministic functions of $s,t,u$, and ${\\mathcal F}_{\\leq s}\\vee {\\mathcal F}_{\\geq u}$ denotes the $\\sigma$-field generated by $\\{X_r: r \\leq s \\text{ or } r \\geq u\\}$. A consequence of this assumption is the relation\n$$E(X_s|{{\\mathcal F}}_{\\ge t}) = \\frac{s}{t}X_t, \\quad \\text{for } s<t.$$\n\nBy assumption, for any $0<s<t$ the conditional second moment is quadratic in $X_t$, i.e.,\n\\begin{equation}\nE(X_s^2|{\\mathcal F}_{\\ge t})=m(s,t)X_t^2+n(s,t)X_t+o(s,t), \\tag{3}\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $m$, $n$, $o$ are some functions.\n\nWe also assume that for any $t>0$, the random variables $1, X_t, X_t^2$ are linearly independent.\n## Theorem\n**Proposition: The structure of reversed conditional second moments.**\nLet $(X_t)_{t\\geq0}$ be a stochastic process satisfying the conditions in the Setup. Then there are constants $0\\leq \\tau<\\infty$ and $-\\infty<\\theta<\\infty$ such that for any $0\\le s<t$, the conditional second moment is given by\n$$\nE(X_s^2|{{\\mathcal F}}_{\\ge t})=\\frac{s(s+\\tau)}{t(t+\\tau)}X_t^2+\\frac{s(t-s)}{t(t+\\tau)}\\theta X_t+\\frac{s(t-s)}{t+\\tau}.\n$$\nAlternatively, in the case corresponding to $\\tau=\\infty$, the conditional second moment is given by\n$$\nE(X_s^2|{{\\mathcal F}}_{\\ge t})=\\frac{s}{t}X_t^2+\\frac{s(t-s)}{t}\\theta X_t.\n$$', 'status': 'ACCEPT', 'result': {'status': 'ACCEPT', 'rejection_reason': None, 'justification': 'This is a legitimate mathematical proof problem about stochastic processes with all necessary setup and context provided. The prompt asks for a mathematical derivation/proof based on explicitly stated assumptions and properties of a specific class of stochastic processes. No images, PII, real-time data, or unsafe content is involved.'}, 'accepted': True, 'error': None, 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1081, 'output_tokens': 87, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003206}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003206}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1081, 'output_tokens': 87, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003206}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003206}}] 
