2026-03-25 08:47:53,546 494048 INFO ? odoo.addons.preference_ranking.models.models: tasks1_response---------------------------[{'index': 0, 'prompt': "You are given a setup and statement to prove or derive. Your job is to provide a complete and correct proof. Think carefully, trying multiple approaches if you are stuck, and finally give a cleaned up proof under the heading ## Proof. If you are unable to complete the proof, be honest and say so.\n\n## Setup\nWe consider a numerical scheme for approximating a density $\\rho$. The one-dimensional computational domain is divided into uniform cells $C_i$, and we denote the cell average on $C_i$ at time step $n$ by $\\rho_i^n$. No-flux boundary conditions are assumed at the boundaries.\n\nThe scheme is defined as follows:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{\\rho_i^{n+1}-\\rho_i^{n}}{\\Delta t}+\\frac{F_{i+1/2}^{n+1}-F_{i-1/2}^{n+1}}{\\Delta x}=0, \\\\\n&F_{i+1/2}^{n+1}= \\rho_i^{n+1}(u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^+ + \\rho_{i+1}^{n+1}(u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^-, \\\\\n&(u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^+=\\max(u_{i+1/2}^{n+1},0), \\quad (u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^-=\\min(u_{i+1/2}^{n+1},0), \\\\\n&u_{i+1/2}^{n+1}=-\\frac{\\xi_{i+1}^{n+1}-\\xi_i^{n+1}}{\\Delta x}, \\\\\n&\\xi_i^{n+1}=H'(\\rho_i^{n+1})+V_i+(W\\ast\\rho^{**})_i,\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nfor a symmetric potential $W$. Here, $\\rho^{**}$ may be chosen as $\\rho^{n}$, $\\rho^{n+1}$, or $(\\rho^{n+1}+\\rho^{n})/{2}$. The confining potential terms are defined as $V_i=V(x_i)$, where $x_i$ is the cell centre, and the convolution is given by $(W\\ast\\rho^{**})_i=\\sum_{k=1}^{2M}W_{i-k}\\rho_k^{**}\\Delta x$, where $W_{i-k}=W(x_i-x_k)$ and $2M$ is the total number of cells.\n## Theorem\nThe scheme defined in the setup is unconditionally positivity preserving: if $\\rho_i^{n}\\geq 0$ for all $i$, then $\\rho_i^{n+1}\\geq 0$ for all $i$.", 'status': 'ACCEPT', 'result': {'status': 'ACCEPT', 'rejection_reason': None, 'justification': 'This is a legitimate mathematical proof request in numerical analysis. The prompt provides complete setup with all necessary equations, definitions, and the theorem to prove. It contains no images, missing references, safety concerns, PII, or real-time data requirements. The content is coherent academic mathematics about proving positivity preservation of a numerical scheme for PDEs.'}, 'accepted': True, 'error': None, 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1020, 'output_tokens': 312, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.005784}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.005784}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1020, 'output_tokens': 312, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.005784}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.005784}}] 
