ccuracy, completeness, or presentation style; both correctly prove P(n) true for infinitely many n via the 2^k - k construction and false for infinitely many n via the sparsity of 7-smooth numbers in short intervals.'}, 'rubrics_vs_gemini': [{'name': 'Explicit arithmetic progression for false case', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explicitly identifies a specific infinite arithmetic progression (n ≡ 4 mod 10 or n = 10m + 4) for which P(n) is false, with concrete verification for n=24, rather than just proving existence of infinitely many false n without a concrete AP.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Concrete impossibility demonstration', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro provides explicit exhaustive verification showing n=24 is impossible by enumerating 7-smooth candidates and their corresponding n values, demonstrating concrete impossibility rather than only asymptotic density arguments.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'LaTeX formatting consistency', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro maintains consistent LaTeX delimiters ($...$ and $$...$$) throughout mathematical expressions, while the SxS winner has formatting inconsistencies (unescaped parentheses in section headers, mixed delimiters).', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Structural section headers', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro uses clear hierarchical section headers with visual separation (###) and descriptive titles, while the SxS winner uses numbered sections with less visual distinction and occasional formatting artifacts.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Density argument completeness', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly states that the arithmetic density of valid n is 0 and explains why this guarantees infinitely many false n in any infinite AP, making the logical connection between density and the conclusion more explicit than the SxS winner's counting argument.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 22899, 'output_tokens': 3234, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.084606}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.084606}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 22899, 'output_tokens': 3234, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.084606}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.084606}}] 
