ially better', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Explicit construction of all 12 post-measurement states', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly lists all 12 king-induced states |Ψ_{m,k}⟩ for m∈{0,1,2,3} and k∈{0,1,2} with their tensor product structure, showing how complex conjugation relates the bases.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: how well this aspect was performed in the comparison', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Complete explicit enumeration of measurement basis vectors', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 writes out all 9 basis vectors |P_0⟩ through |P_8⟩ explicitly with their components in the A_0⊗A_0 basis, not just the general formula.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: how well this aspect was performed in the comparison', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Decoding table for all four observables', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 provides a clear table (equation 6) showing the linear congruence condition for nonzero overlap for each of the four observables m=0,1,2,3.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: how well this aspect was performed in the comparison', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit verification with concrete numerical example', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 includes a complete worked example verifying the protocol for the specific case m=1, k=2, computing actual inner products and confirming the decoding rule.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: how well this aspect was performed in the comparison', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Information-theoretic optimality proof', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 proves that 9 basis states are necessary (not just sufficient) via counting argument using incidence bounds, showing N≥9 is required.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: how well this aspect was performed in the comparison', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Clear modular section headers', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 uses descriptive hierarchical headers (## Strategy, ## Step 1, ## Step 2, etc.) that structure the proof into logical, navigable components.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: how well this aspect was performed in the comparison', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit handlin