robability verification step.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Correct handling of complex conjugation for MUBs', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro correctly identifies and handles the complex conjugate relationships between $A_1$ and $A_2$ bases ($|1_k^*\\rangle = |2_k\\rangle$) and the permutation structure of $A_3$ ($|3_k^*\\rangle = |3_{-k}\\rangle$), while the SxS winner obscures this structure in generic unitary notation.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'LaTeX formatting quality', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro uses proper LaTeX delimiters ($...$) with correct spacing and alignment, while the SxS winner uses inconsistent spacing (e.g., $\\;|\\Psi _0\\rangle =...\\;\\tag{1}$ with awkward semicolon spacing) and has formatting artifacts.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Explicit construction of all 12 post-measurement states', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly lists all 12 possible king-induced states |Ψ_{m,k}⟩ in equation (3), showing the pattern of complex conjugation across the four MUBs, while the SxS winner only describes them generically.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = marginally better enumeration, 3-4 = clear explicit listing with pattern identification, 5-6 = complete explicit construction with structural insight', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit formula for measurement basis with index structure', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 provides the explicit formula |P_{u,v}⟩ = (1/√3)Σ_j x^{vj}|0_j 0_{u-j}⟩ in equation (4) with clear (u,v) labeling, while the SxS winner uses Bell state notation |P_{a,b}⟩ = (I⊗X^aZ^b)|Ψ_0⟩ without explicit component expansion.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = slightly more explicit, 3-4 = clearly more explicit with component-level