nwhere $M_{S,2}$ is the set of functions from $S$ to $\\{\\pm 1\\}$ and $M_{T,2}$ is the set of functions from $T$ to $\\{\\pm 1\\}$.\n\nThe max-norm of a function (or matrix) $Z: S \\times T \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ is defined as:\n$$\n\\|Z\\|_{\\max}=\\min_{Z=UV^{\\top}}\\max(\\|U\\|^2_{2,\\infty},\\|V\\|^2_{2,\\infty})\n$$\nwhere $U$ and $V$ can be thought of as mappings from $S$ and $T$ respectively into a Hilbert space, such that $Z(x,y)=\\langle U(x),V(y)\\rangle$. The term $\\|U\\|_{2,\\infty}$ is the maximum $\\ell_2$ norm of the vectors $U(x)$ over all $x \\in S$, i.e. $\\|U\\|_{2,\\infty}=\\sup_x \\|U(x)\\|_2$.\n## Theorem\nFor any two sets $S$ and $T$ of objects and any function $\\text{sim}:S\\times T \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$, we have that $\\|sim\\|_{\\max} \\leq \\rho_2(sim)$ and the inequality is tight.', 'status': 'ACCEPT', 'result': {'status': 'ACCEPT', 'rejection_reason': None, 'justification': 'The user has provided a clear mathematical theorem to prove, with complete setup including definitions of asymmetric clustering, convex hull relaxation, binary cluster ratio, and max-norm. All necessary mathematical objects and notation are explicitly defined within the prompt. This is a legitimate mathematical proof request with no safety concerns, no missing references, and no other rejection criteria apply.'}, 'accepted': True, 'error': None, 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1283, 'output_tokens': 98, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003742}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.003742}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 1283, 'output_tokens': 98, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.003742}, 'total_