struction Following, Truthfulness, Prompt Correctness, Writing Style, and Verbosity metrics: the SxS winner response contains the exact same proof strategy, step-by-step derivation of sideband phases (φ_rsb = θ_A - θ_Br, φ_bsb = θ_Bb - θ_A), cancellation of θ_A terms, final expression φ_G = θ_Br - θ_Bb, and residual sensitivity formula δφ_G = (k_B,r - k_B,b)δx as the GPT 5.2 response. Both correctly identify the geometric phase insensitivity mechanism where opposite absorption/emission roles of k_A in red vs blue sidebands cause exact cancellation. Both conclude with the same boxed residual sensitivity formula and identical explanatory text. No discernible difference exists in scientific accuracy, logical flow, LaTeX formatting, or completeness of the proof.'}, 'rubrics_vs_gemini': [{'name': 'LaTeX equation formatting', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro uses proper LaTeX display math delimiters ($$...$$) for all equations, while the SxS winner uses inconsistent formatting (some display math, some inline).', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 for minor LaTeX issues, 3-4 for noticeable formatting problems, 5-6 for substantially cleaner LaTeX rendering', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit absorption/emission sign convention', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explicitly states the physical sign convention (absorption adds phase, emission subtracts phase) before applying it, while the SxS winner assumes this convention without stating it.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 for minor clarity difference, 3-4 for noticeable pedagogical gap, 5-6 for critical missing explanation', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Numbered proof steps', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro uses explicit numbered steps (1, 2, 3, 4) in the proof section, while the SxS winner uses descriptive subsection headers without sequential numbering.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 for minor organizational difference, 3-4 for clearer structure, 5-6 for substantially better logical flow', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Final conclusion marker', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro includes a clear end-of-proof marker ($\\blacksquare$) after the final conclusion, while the SxS winner lacks any explicit proof termination symbol.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 for minor presentational difference, 3-4 for noticeable completeness gap, 5-6 for substantially more professional formatting', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Physical justification for wave number approximation', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly justifies why $k_{B,r} \\approx k_{B,b}$ (same atomic transition), while the SxS winner only cites the setup's approximation without physical reasoning.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 for minor depth difference, 3-4 for noticeable explanatory gap, 5-6 for critical missing physical insight', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 22271, 'output_tokens': 2742, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.077446}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.077446}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 22271, 'output_tokens': 2742, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.077446}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.077446}}] 
