etter with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit cancellation mechanism explanation', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly notes that φ_G is independent of θ_A and explains why (absorption/emission roles of k_A are opposite), while the SxS winner shows this algebraically without explicitly highlighting this physical interpretation.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Boxed final verification formula', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 uses LaTeX boxing (\\boxed{}) for the key residual sensitivity formula in the verification section, making the final result visually prominent, while the SxS winner presents the same formula without special formatting.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Consistent mathematical notation', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 uses consistent subscript notation (θ_{B_r}, θ_{B_b}) throughout, while the SxS winner mixes φ_{B,r} and φ_{B,b} with φ_{rsb}, φ_{bsb} without clear notational hierarchy.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}, {'name': 'Explicit assumption statement', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly states the assumption that θ_A is not affected by the common-mode fluctuation, while the SxS winner does not explicitly state this assumption.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 3}], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 22897, 'output_tokens': 3491, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.087686}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.087686}, 'token_u