ession."}}, {'rubric_name': 'Coefficient Identification and Sign Verification', 'opalite': {'score': 6, 'reason': "The proof explicitly identifies coefficients under 'Coefficients': diagonal a_{ii} = 1 + Δt/Δx((u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^+ + |(u_{i-1/2}^{n+1})^-|) > 0, and off-diagonal a_{i,i-1} = -Δt/Δx(u_{i-1/2}^{n+1})^+ ≤ 0, a_{i,i+1} = Δt/Δx(u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^- ≤ 0. Each sign is verified using the definitions of (u)^+ and (u)^-. No faults found."}, 'ophelia': {'score': 6, 'reason': 'The proof explicitly identifies coefficients with a case structure: the diagonal coefficient is shown to be 1+λ((u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^+ + |(u_{i-1/2}^{n+1})^-|) > 0, and the off-diagonal contributions λ(u_{i-1/2}^{n+1})^+ ≥ 0 and -λ(u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^- = λ|(u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^-| ≥ 0 are verified. The matrix entries M_{i,i-1} = -λ(u_{i-1/2}^{n+1})^+ ≤ 0 and M_{i,i+1} = λ(u_{i+1/2}^{n+1})^- ≤ 0 are explicitly stated and verified. No faults found.'}, 'gemini': {'score': 6, 'reason': "The proof has a dedicated section '2. Identifying Coefficients and Verifying Signs' that explicitly defines C_i, a_i, b_i and verifies: C_i ≥ 1 > 0, a_i ≥ 0, b_i ≥ 0. It then notes that the coefficients multiplying ρ_{i+1}^{n+1} and ρ_{i-1}^{n+1} on the RHS (a_i/C_i and b_i/C_i) are non-negative. The signs are verified using the definitions of (u)^+ and (u)^-. No faults found."}, 'gpt': {'score': 6, 'reason': "The proof explicitly identifies: A_{i,i} = 1+λ(u_{i+1/2}^+ - u_{i-1/2}^-), A_{i,i-1} = -λu_{i-1/2}^+, A_{i,i+1} = λu_{i+1/2}^-. Under 'Sign of coefficients' it verifies: A_{i,i} > 0, A_{i,i-1} ≤ 0, A_{i,i+1} ≤ 0 using u^+ ≥ 0 and u^- ≤ 0. The verification is clear and complete. No faults found."}}, {'rubric_name': 'No-Flux Boundary Conditions Explanation', 'opalite': {'score': 5, 'reason': "The proof has a dedicated 'Boundary cells' paragraph that explains: 'The no-flux condition gives u_{1/2}^{n+1}=u_{2M+1/2}^{n+1}=0. Hence the terms involving ρ_0^{n+1} and ρ_{2M+1}^{n+1} vanish in (1) for i=1 and i=2M; the same sign 