ptions (convergence / operator inverses)' subsection that explicitly states technical assumptions about convergence, boundary conditions, and invertibility of operators.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = implicit assumptions only, 3-4 = some assumptions mentioned in passing, 5-6 = dedicated labeled subsection with comprehensive assumptions', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Measure preservation explicitly justified', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 provides explicit discretization argument showing the Jacobian is unity via triangular matrix structure, with explicit matrix form shown.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = assertion of unit Jacobian, 3-4 = brief justification, 5-6 = explicit discretization argument with matrix structure displayed', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Step-by-step parameter derivation', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 derives parameters (κ, m̃, B̃, θ̃) through explicit completing-the-square steps with intermediate equations tagged (3.1)-(3.8), showing how each emerges from the transformation.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = final values stated, 3-4 = some derivation steps, 5-6 = complete step-by-step derivation with tagged equations for each parameter', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Explicit operator Δ construction', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly constructs the operator Δ through intermediate operators D, D̄ with explicit differential forms (5.1)-(5.2), rather than asserting its form.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = Δ stated without construction, 3-4 = brief motivation, 5-6 = explicit construction from first-order differential operators with normalization', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Independent verification section', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a dedicated 'Independent check of the final quadratic source term' section that verifies the residue formula by computing [Δ, Δ̄] = 0 and explicit operator product.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = no verification, 3-4 = brief consistency check, 5-6 = dedicated section with explicit computation verifying commutation and operator product', 'rating': 6}, 