ent matching in functional equations', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explicitly labels and derives the three coefficient equations (A1-A3, C1-C3) with clear algebraic steps, while the SxS winner presents the same equations with less explicit derivation', 'scale': '1-6 scale: how clearly the coefficient matching process is demonstrated step-by-step', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Dual method derivation for cross-moment', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro computes E(X_s X_t | F_{≥u}) through two distinct methods (conditioning on F_{≥t} first vs F_{≤s} ∨ F_{≥u} first) and explicitly labels them Method 1 and Method 2, while the SxS winner uses a less direct approach via the linear regression residual', 'scale': '1-6 scale: clarity and completeness of the dual derivation approach', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit solution for n(s,t) via H(t) function', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro introduces an auxiliary function H(t) and explicitly solves for it through algebraic manipulation of the functional equations, while the SxS winner uses a less direct substitution with p(s,t) and ψ(t)', 'scale': '1-6 scale: clarity of the explicit solution pathway for n(s,t)', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Verification of consistency equation (C3)', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explicitly verifies that equation (C3) for o(s,t) is satisfied by the derived solution, while the SxS winner does not explicitly check this consistency condition', 'scale': '1-6 scale: completeness of verification steps', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Handling of τ = ∞ limiting case', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explicitly treats the τ = ∞ case as a separate limit with C=0, showing the derivation steps, while the SxS winner mentions it more briefly without explicit limiting analysis', 'scale': '1-6 scale: explicitness of the limiting case analysis', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Explicit verification of normalization', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 includes explicit verification that E(E(X_s^2|F_{≥t})) = s at the end of the proof, che