n by\n$$\nE(X_s^2|{{\\mathcal F}}_{\\ge t})=\\frac{s(s+\\tau)}{t(t+\\tau)}X_t^2+\\frac{s(t-s)}{t(t+\\tau)}\\theta X_t+\\frac{s(t-s)}{t+\\tau}.\n$$\nAlternatively, in the case corresponding to $\\tau=\\infty$, the conditional second moment is given by\n$$\nE(X_s^2|{{\\mathcal F}}_{\\ge t})=\\frac{s}{t}X_t^2+\\frac{s(t-s)}{t}\\theta X_t.\n$$', 'evaluation_result': {'response_a': {'instruction_following': {'score': 6, 'reason': 'All instruction elements satisfied: (1) Complete proof provided under ## Proof heading; (2) Multiple approaches used (tower property, coefficient matching, functional equations); (3) Honest completion with no admission of inability needed. Checklist: [X] Proof heading present, [X] Complete derivation of both cases (τ<∞ and τ=∞), [X] All coefficients m,n,o determined, [X] Verification of variance non-negativity included, [X] Cleaned up final presentation. No unrequested content added, no formatting violations.'}, 'truthfulness': {'score': 5, 'reason': "All major mathematical claims verified: [VERIFIED] m(s,t)=h(s)/h(t) from multiplicative property (Cauchy-type functional equation); [VERIFIED] Jensen functional equation g(t)(u-s)=(u-t)g(s)+(t-s)g(u) with affine solutions; [VERIFIED] Variance calculation showing τ≥0 requirement; [VERIFIED] Final forms match theorem statement exactly. One [UNVERIFIABLE] claim: 'Multiplying h by a constant does not change m' is technically verifiable but trivial. No [FALSE] or [QUESTIONABLE] claims identified. The derivation of o(s,t)=s-t·m(s,t) from expectations is correct: E[E(X_s²|F_{≥t})]=E[X_s²]=s, and E[m(s,t)X_t²+n(s,t)X_t+o(s,t)]=m(s,t)t+o(s,t), so o(s,t)=s-t·m(s,t)."}, 'prompt_correctness': {'score': 6, 'reason': 'Correctness audit: [CORRECT] Derivation of m(s,t) yielding s(s+τ)/[t(t+τ)] or s/t; [CORRECT] Derivation of n(s,t) with θ parameter; [CORRECT] Derivation of o(s,t) as s(t-s)/(t+τ) or 0; [CORRECT] Both cases (τ<∞ and τ=∞) fully covered; [CORRECT] All assumptions (1),(2),(3) and linear independence used appropriately; [CORRECT] Final conclusion matches theorem statement exactly. No [PARTIALLY CORRECT], [INCORRECT], or [MISSING] elements.'}, 'writing_style': {'score': 5, 'reason': "Professional mathematical writing with clear structure. Minor issue identified: use of '\\t' instead of '\\tfrac' or '\\frac' in some places (e.g., '\\tfrac{t}{u}') and inconsistent spacing around '\\mid' in conditional expectations. The proof flows logically with numbered sections. One trivial style preference: could use more explicit justification for why r(s,t)=f(t)-f(s) form follows from additive property, though standard. Overall: publication-ready with only cosmetic variations."}, 'verbosity': {'score': 5, 'reason': 'Length analysis: Nothing can be cut because each section serves essential purpose—Section 1 establishes composition rules, Section 2 derives cross-moment constraints, Sections 3-5 solve for each coefficient. Nothing is missing because all steps from assumptions to conclusion are present. Near-perfect calibration: only trivial trimming possible (e.g., the explicit verification of (C3) at the end could be slightly condensed, but provides valuable consistency check).'}, 'overall_quality': {'weighted_score': 5.45, 'reason': 'Weighted: IF×0.25 + Truth×0.25 + Correctness×0.20 + Writing×0.15 + Verbosity×0.15 = 5.45'}}, 'response_b': {'instruction_following': {'score': 4, 'reason': "Checklist analysis: [X] Proof heading present; [X] Multiple approaches attempted; [X] Both τ cases covered; [X] Final forms match theorem. However: [ ] Contains 'Outline of Strategy' section before proof—unrequested content that adds ~15% length; [ ] Has typographical errors ('Thisimmediately', 'conditioning firston', 'F_{\\get}', 'F_{\\les}', 'F_{\\geu}') that suggest insufficient cleanup; [ ] Step 5 verification is incomplete (claims 'certifying completely congruent internal mechanics' without full clarity). The outline section, while helpful, was not requested and violates 'cleaned up proof' 