cit verification step checking that equation (C3) is satisfied by the derived expressions, whereas the SxS winner states the final form without this verification.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = no verification, 3-4 = brief mention of consistency, 5-6 = explicit computational verification of consistency conditions', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Intermediate algebraic simplification shown', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro displays intermediate algebraic steps when solving for H(t), showing 'The grouped bracket reduces natively to...', while the SxS winner jumps from the functional equation to the solution.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = algebraic steps omitted, 3-4 = some steps shown, 5-6 = explicit demonstration of algebraic simplification', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Physical interpretation of parameter constraints', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro includes the phrase 'where τ ≥ 0 maps to physical variance bounds where conditions are strictly positive' explaining the constraint on τ, while the SxS winner only states 'forces τ ≥ 0' without motivation.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = constraint stated without context, 3-4 = brief motivation, 5-6 = explicit connection to physical/probabilistic interpretation', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Explicit strategy outline before proof', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a clearly labeled 'Strategy (outline)' section with numbered steps before the formal ## Proof heading, explaining the proof approach at a high level.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = brief mention of approach, 3-4 = clear outline with some structure, 5-6 = comprehensive roadmap with numbered steps covering all major proof phases', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'LaTeX equation alignment and display formatting', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 uses proper LaTeX display environments with aligned equations, boxed results for key equations (M), (N), (O), (M2), (N2), (O2), and consistent spacing between display math and text.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = basic inline math, 3-4 = some display 