2026-03-25 09:16:00,659 494048 INFO ? odoo.addons.preference_ranking.models.models: eval_oph response: [{'task_id': 'tv_stem_6572', 'prompt': 'You are given a setup and statement to prove or derive. Your job is to provide a complete and correct proof. Think carefully, trying multiple approaches if you are stuck, and finally give a cleaned up proof under the heading ## Proof. If you are unable to complete the proof, be honest and say so.\n\n## Setup\nWe are concerned with solving the following three-by-three block system of linear equations\n$$\n\\mathcal{B} x \\equiv\\left(\\begin{array}{ccc}\n{A} & {B^{T}} & {0} \\\\\n{-B} & {0} & {-C^{T}} \\\\\n{0} & {C} & {0}\n\\end{array}\\right)\\left(\\begin{array}{l}\n{x} \\\\\n{y} \\\\\n{z}\n\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{c}\n{f} \\\\\n{-g} \\\\\n{h}\n\\end{array}\\right)=b,\n$$\nwhere $A\\in \\mathbb{R}^{n\\times n}$ is a symmetric positive definite (SPD), $B\\in \\mathbb{R}^{m\\times n}$ and $C\\in \\mathbb{R}^{l\\times m}$ have full row rank. We assume that $n \\geq m$ and $m \\geq l.$\n\nWe split the coefficient matrix $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathcal{B}=\\mathcal{P}-\\mathcal{R},$ where\n$$\\mathcal{P}=\\left(\\begin{array}\n{ccc}\nA & B^{T} & 0 \\\\\n0 & \\alpha I+ \\beta B B^{T} & -C^{T} \\\\\n0 & 0 & \\alpha I+ \\beta C C^{T}\n\\end{array}\\right),$$\nand $\\mathcal{R} = \\mathcal{P} - \\mathcal{B}$, i.e.,\n$$ \\mathcal{R}=\\left(\\begin{array}\n{ccc}\n0 & 0 & 0 \\\\\nB & \\alpha I+ \\beta B B^{T} & 0 \\\\\n0 & -C & \\alpha I+ \\beta C C^{T}\n\\end{array}\\right),$$\nin which $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are given positive constants. The matrix $\\mathcal{P}$ is nonsingular. The iterative scheme associated with this splitting can be constructed as\n$$\n{x}^{(k+1)}= \\mathcal{G}_{\\alpha,\\beta} {x}^{(k)}+ f, k=0,1,2,\\dots,\n$$\nwhere $x^{(0)}$ is arbitrary, $\\mathcal{G}_{\\alpha,\\beta}= \\mathcal{P}^{-1} \\mathcal{R}$ is the iteration matrix and $f=\\mathcal{P}^{-1} {b}.$\n\nFor a given matrix $M$ with real eigenvalues, $\\lambda_{\\min}(M)$ and $\\lambda_{\\max}(M)$ stand for the minimum and maximum eigenvalue of $M,$ respectively. The minimum and maximum singular value of $M$ are represented by $\\sigma_{\\min}(M)$ and $\\sigma_{\\max}(M)$, respectively. For any arbitrary complex vectors $x,$ $x^{H}$ indicates the conjugate transpose of $x$.\n\nThe proof of the theorem requires the following lemma.\n\n**Lemma** [28] Consider the quadratic equation $x^{2} - b x +c=0,$ where $b$ and $c$ are real numbers. Both roots of the equation are less than one in modulus if and only if $|c| < 1$ and $|b| < 1+c.$\n## Theorem\n**Theorem 1** Suppose that $A\\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times n}$ is SPD, $B \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$ and $C \\in \\mathbb{R}^{l \\times m}$ are full row rank matrices. Then, the iterative method\n$$\n{x}^{(k+1)}= \\mathcal{G}_{\\alpha,\\beta} {x}^{(k)}+ f, k=0,1,2,\\dots,\n$$\nconverges to the unique solution of the system $\\mathcal{B}x=b$ for any initial guess, if\n$$\n\\frac{{{\\sigma_{\\max}}^{2} (C)}}{\\alpha+\\beta {\\sigma_{\\min}}^{2}(C^{T})} +2 \\frac{ {{\\sigma_{\\max}}^{2} ( B^{T})}}{\\lambda_{\\min} (A)} < 4 (\\alpha +\\beta {\\sigma_{\\min}}^{2} ( B^{T})).\n$$', 'evaluation_result': {'response_a': {'instruction_following': {'score': 4, 'reason': "The response provides a complete proof under the ## Proof heading as requested. However, it adds substantial unrequested content in Sections 5 and 6 ('Two-block case C=0' and 'Effect of α,β'), which go beyond proving the theorem to include discussion and analysis. The prompt asks only to 'provide a complete and correct proof' with honesty if unable to complete. The additional sections are not part of the proof itself but commentary. This triggers the 'Adding unrequested content → -1 point' deduction, capping at score 4. Checklist: [X] Provide proof under ## Proof heading; [X] Attempt to prove the theorem; [X] Be honest if unable; [ ] Do not add unnecessary analysis beyond proof (FAILED - Sections 5-6 are e