inear Diophantine equation 47A - 43C = 1 via the extended Euclidean algorithm, yielding smaller denominators (43 and 47 vs. 172 and 188).', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = marginally better approach, 3-4 = noticeably more elegant with clear mathematical advantage, 5-6 = substantially superior method producing optimal denominators', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Extended Euclidean algorithm shown', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly displays the full extended Euclidean algorithm with forward steps and back-substitution to solve 47A - 43C = 1, while the SxS winner skips this algorithmic technique entirely.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minor algorithmic detail present, 3-4 = clear algorithmic demonstration, 5-6 = complete, instructive algorithmic exposition that the SxS winner lacks', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Optimal denominator minimization', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 achieves denominators 43 and 47 (the prime factors themselves), which are the smallest possible denominators under 2021, while the SxS winner produces larger denominators 172 and 188.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = slightly smaller denominators, 3-4 = significantly smaller denominators, 5-6 = minimal possible denominators demonstrating mathematical optimality', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Structured section headers', 'description': "GPT 5.2 uses consistent markdown headers (###, ##) with descriptive titles ('Search strategy (brief)', 'Step-by-step algebra', 'Verification of the subtraction', 'Irreducibility checks') to organize the solution flow.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = basic headers present, 3-4 = clear hierarchical organization, 5-6 = exemplary structural navigation that enhances readability', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit verification step', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a dedicated 'Verification of the subtraction' section that explicitly computes 11·47 - 12·43 = 517 - 516 = 1, while the SxS winner embeds verification within the algebraic work.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = verification mentioned, 3-4 = clear 