 clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Strategic overview section', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a dedicated 'Strategy' section that outlines the proof structure, constructs the candidate extension F, and lists the classical tools to be used before diving into technical details, which the SxS winner lacks entirely.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit discussion of where boundedness is used', 'description': "GPT 5.2 contains a dedicated section titled 'Where boundedness of f is essential (and what fails without it)' that explicitly identifies the critical role of boundedness and provides a concrete counterexample (f(z)=1/z), which the SxS winner omits.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Clear statement of independence from auxiliary domain choice', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly proves that the continuation is well-defined independent of the choice of auxiliary domain D by invoking the identity theorem, whereas the SxS winner does not address this potential ambiguity.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Proper LaTeX formatting for mathematical expressions', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 uses consistent LaTeX formatting with proper display math environments, aligned equations, and readable spacing, while the SxS winner uses plain TeX-style $$ delimiters and cramped formatting.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit handling of the η parameter in approximation', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly introduces and handles the arbitrary η>0 parameter when approximating losc, then takes η↓0, making the approximation argument rigorous and complete, whereas the SxS winner implicitly assumes the infimum is attained.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 23963, 'output_tokens': 4425, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.101026}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.101026}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 23963, 'output_tokens': 4425, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.101026}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.101026}}] 
