plicitly defines Q as the ideal generated by quadratic binomials in J_{B_ell} and proves equality J_{B_ell} = Q, whereas the SxS winner only shows quadratic equivalence without this algebraic framing.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Clear telescoping sum argument', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly writes out the telescoping sum (P^{T_0}-P^{T_1}) + ... + (P^{T_{m-1}}-P^{T_m}) = P^T-P^S to show the generator lies in Q, while the SxS winner never makes this algebraic decomposition explicit.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Factorization of Plücker monomials M_r', 'description': "GPT 5.2 explicitly identifies the common factor M_r of unchanged columns in each quadratic swap, showing P^{T_{r-1}} - P^{T_r} = M_r(P_C P_D - P_{C'}P_{D'}), which the SxS winner omits entirely.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Proper LaTeX display math environments', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 uses proper LaTeX display environments with \\[...\\] and aligned equations for the telescoping sum and factorization, while the SxS winner uses informal \\medskip\\noindent\\textbf{} formatting with inline math.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit verification that quadratic binomials generate', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly proves both inclusions Q ⊆ J_{B_ell} and J_{B_ell} ⊆ Q with clear logical structure, while the SxS winner only argues equivalence of tableaux without proving ideal equality.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Avoidance of unnecessary induction', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 gives a direct proof using the Grassman