s mentioned briefly, 3-4 if clearly stated with brief justification, 5-6 if fully formalized with proofs', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Claim-based proof structure', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 organizes the proof into numbered, titled claims with explicit justifications, while the SxS winner presents the same reasoning in continuous prose without explicit claim demarcation.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 if some claims present, 3-4 if clear claim/justification structure, 5-6 if rigorous claim-based structure throughout', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Multiplicity of puncturing factor calculated', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 includes Claim 2 explicitly computing mult_v(B) = |v| for the puncturing factor B, while the SxS winner computes this implicitly during analysis without explicit statement.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 if mentioned in passing, 3-4 if calculated explicitly, 5-6 if formalized as standalone claim with proof', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'General constraint formula derived', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 derives the general formula mult_v(u) ≥ 3-|v| for all v ∈ Q^n\\{0} before specializing, while the SxS winner derives constraints only for specific cases (|v|=1 and |v|=2) without the general pattern.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 if pattern suggested, 3-4 if formula stated, 5-6 if formula derived and then specialized', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Polynomial simplification to closed form', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly simplifies the constrained quadratic u to the closed form c(∑x_i - 1)^2 using the substitution s = ∑x_i, while the SxS winner solves the linear system without showing this structural simplification.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 if simplification mentioned, 3-4 if algebraic simplification shown, 5-6 if elegant closed form derived with substitution', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Hyperplane scaling normalization', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly scales each L_j so that L_j(0) = 1, making P(0) = 1 transparent, while the SxS winner states f(0) ≠ 0 without this normalization step.',