planation with concrete counterexample mechanism', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro explains why k=1 fails by analyzing how M_{n+1}(c) drops from 1 to 0 and the frequency must jump, while the SxS winner only gives a concrete example without explaining the structural mechanism.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 slightly better explanation, 3-4 clearly deeper structural insight, 5-6 substantially more illuminating mathematical analysis', 'rating': 4}], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Explicit liminf definition and usage', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly defines m := liminf a_n and uses this formal definition to establish that all sufficiently late terms satisfy a_n ≥ m and that m occurs infinitely often, whereas the SxS winner does not introduce this formal analytical tool.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Rigorous contradiction proof that sequence is bounded', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 provides a complete proof by contradiction that a_n cannot tend to infinity, using the explicit bound A := max(N, a_1, ..., a_N) and showing f_k(n) ≤ A for large n, while the SxS winner assumes finiteness without proof.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit construction of stabilization point', 'description': "GPT 5.2 explicitly constructs n_0 as the first index > N satisfying two concrete conditions (a_{n_0} = m and c_m(n_0-1) > m), proving existence and well-definedness, while the SxS winner's 'first n ≥ M' construction is less precise about the strict inequality condition.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 marginally better, 3-4 noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 substantially better', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Clear separation of tie-breaking independence', 'description': "GPT 5.2 has a dedicated subsection 'Where does it become constant, and why is that point well-defined?' that e