le': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = implicit handling, 3-4 = mentions ambiguity, 5-6 = rigorous formalization with proof of well-definedness', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Proof that sequence cannot diverge to infinity', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 contains a dedicated Step 2 proving by contradiction that a_n cannot tend to +∞, using the bound A = max(N, a_1, ..., a_N).', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = assumes finiteness, 3-4 = brief justification, 5-6 = complete rigorous proof with explicit contradiction', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Explicit absorbing state identification', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly identifies condition (★): f_k(t)=m and c_m(t)>m, then proves this is an absorbing state that forces constancy.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = implicit in argument, 3-4 = states condition, 5-6 = formally labeled, proven absorbing with inductive continuation', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Well-definedness of stabilization point', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 includes a dedicated section proving the first stabilization index n_0 is well-defined without tie-breaking choices, with explicit verification of independence from tie resolution.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = no discussion, 3-4 = brief mention, 5-6 = thorough analysis with explicit conditions and justification', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Discussion of k=1 boundary case', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 includes a section analyzing why k≥2 hypothesis is stated and notes the proof actually works for k=1, with explanation of intuitive differences.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = no mention, 3-4 = brief note, 5-6 = detailed analysis showing proof generality and explaining hypothesis motivation', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'LaTeX display equation formatting', 'description': "GPT 5.2 uses proper LaTeX display environments with \\[ ... \\] and aligned equations, versus the SxS winner's inline-only formatting.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = minimal display math, 3-4 = some display equations, 5-6 = extensive proper display formatting with aligned structures', 'rating': 5}, {'