2026-03-25 10:32:14,336 494048 INFO ? odoo.addons.preference_ranking.models.models: tasks1_response---------------------------[{'index': 0, 'prompt': 'You are given a setup and statement to prove or derive. Your job is to provide a complete and correct proof. Think carefully, trying multiple approaches if you are stuck, and finally give a cleaned up proof under the heading ## Proof. If you are unable to complete the proof, be honest and say so.\n\n## Setup\nWe consider the lattice $II_{25,1}$. Let $G$ be the Weyl group of $II_{25,1}$ and $w$ be its Weyl vector. Let $D$ be the fundamental domain of $II_{25,1}$.\n\nThe Kac-Weyl formula for a certain graded vector space $M$ with root system in $II_{25,1}$ states that\n$$\n\\prod_r(1-e^r) = \\sum_{\\sigma\\in G}\\det(\\sigma)e^{\\sigma(w)-w}\n$$\nwhere the product is over the roots $r$ of $M$ with $-(r,w)>0$ taken with their multiplicities, and the sum is over the elements $\\sigma$ of the Weyl group $G$.\n\nLet $z$ be a primitive norm 0 vector in $D$ not equal to $w$. Then the Dynkin diagram of $z^\\perp$ is the Dynkin diagram of an affine Lie algebra. By quotienting out part of the center of this Lie algebra and adding an outer derivation we get a Lie algebra $Z$ with Cartan subalgebra $II_{25,1}\\otimes \\R$ whose simple roots are the simple roots of $D$ in $z^\\perp$. Let $H$ be the Weyl group of $z^\\perp$.\n\n$Z$ acts on $M$ by the adjoint representation of $M$ restricted to $Z$ and $Z$ preserves each of the subspaces $M_i$ where $M_i$ is the sum of the roots spaces of $M$ for the roots that have inner product $-i$ with $z$. $M_0$ is the adjoint representation of $Z$, while $M_i$ for $i$ positive is a sum of a finite number of highest weight representations of $Z$.\n\nLet $d$ be the number of simple roots of $D$ with $-(r,z)=1$.\n## Theorem\n$M_1$ considered as a representation of $Z$ is a sum of $d$ irreducible representations whose highest weights are the simple roots $r$ with $-(r,z)=1$.', 'status': 'ACCEPT', '