rbosity includes unnecessary section headers and repetition without adding substantive content."}, 'rubrics_vs_gemini': [{'name': 'I-strain theory citation', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly names and applies Brown's I-strain (internal strain) theory as the explanatory framework.", 'scale': "1-6: 1-2 mentions strain generally, 3-4 mentions I-strain without elaboration, 5-6 fully develops Brown's I-strain theory with specific application to both ring systems", 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Torsional strain analysis in cyclopentanone reactant', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro analyzes how the sp2 carbonyl in cyclopentanone eliminates eclipsing interactions that would exist in a fully saturated five-membered ring.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 no mention, 3-4 brief mention, 5-6 detailed explanation of how sp2 carbonyl relieves torsional strain in the reactant', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Structured section headers', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro uses clear markdown section headers (e.g., 'Thermodynamic Trend:', 'Structural Origin:') to organize the general statement in part (b).", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 no headers, 3-4 some organization, 5-6 explicit labeled sections with consistent formatting', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Numerical angle values for cyclohexanone', 'description': 'Gemini 3 Pro provides specific numerical values for the compressed C-C(=O)-C angle in cyclohexanone (~116°) versus the ideal sp2 angle.', 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 no specific values, 3-4 approximate values, 5-6 precise quantitative values with comparison to ideal geometry', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit thermodynamic vs. kinetic distinction', 'description': "Gemini 3 Pro explicitly labels the general statement as 'Thermodynamic Trend' and discusses equilibrium constants versus rates.", 'scale': '1-6: 1-2 conflates thermodynamics and kinetics, 3-4 mentions both, 5-6 clearly distinguishes and labels thermodynamic versus kinetic aspects', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Formatting consistency for ring size labels', 'description'