licit lemma statements with formal hypotheses', 'description': "GPT 5.2 states Lemmas 1, 2, and 3 with explicit formal hypotheses (e.g., 'Let I^nattheory be any T_ufia-interpretation satisfying AX^full_pow2'), whereas the SxS winner references 'Lemma 0' without stating its hypotheses or giving it a numbered, referenceable form.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1=marginally more explicit, 6=completely formal with all hypotheses stated', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Base case and inductive step explicitly labeled in proofs', 'description': "GPT 5.2 explicitly labels 'Base case k=1' and 'Inductive step' in Lemma 2's proof, while the SxS winner omits explicit structural labels for the induction, only mentioning 'proved by induction on k' without showing the case structure.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1=slightly more labeled, 6=fully explicit case structure', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Termination argument explicitly stated', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes an explicit 'Termination condition' subsection explaining why the recursion terminates ('Each recursive axiom application replaces k by k-1...after k-1 steps we reach the base case'), while the SxS winner does not address termination of the recursive axioms.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1=brief mention, 6=complete termination argument', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Construction of counterexample interpretation detailed step-by-step', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 enumerates four explicit steps for constructing I^nattheory in the (<=) direction (integers/arithmetic, free parameters, translated variables, uninterpreted functions), while the SxS winner presents the construction in a single paragraph without numbered steps.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1=slightly more structured, 6=fully explicit enumerated construction', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit justification for why restrictions matter', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a dedicated subsection 'Why the restrictions (no extract, no concrete constants) matter' with two bullet points explaining each restriction, while the SxS winner only mentions the restriction in the final sentence without explanatory justification.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1=brief mention, 6=detailed explanatory section', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Proof strategy overview before technical details', 'description': "GPT 5.2 begins with a 'Proof strategy' subsection outlining the high-level approach before diving into lemmas, while the SxS winner immediately starts with technical definitions without strategic overview.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1=minimal overview, 6=comprehensive strategic roadmap', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit notation section defining all symbols used', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a 'Notation and semantics used' subsection with formal definitions of bw_J, val_J, and the interpretation brackets, while the SxS winner uses similar notation without explicit definition.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1=some definitions, 6=complete notational glossary', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Structural headings for proof directions', 'description': "GPT 5.2 uses explicit LaTeX-style headings '## (=>)' and '## (<=)' with clear directional labels, while the SxS winner uses bold text markers without hierarchical section structure.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1=slightly clearer, 6=formal hierarchical structure', 'rating': 3}], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 41815, 'output_tokens': 4028, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.131966}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.131966}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 41815, 'output_tokens': 4028, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.131966}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.131966}}] 
