 step proof for Lemma 2 (bitwise AND/XOR correctness), including explicit termination justification, while the SxS winner merely asserts 'Lemma 0 (proved by induction on k)' without any proof details.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = external model provides slightly more detail; 3-4 = external model provides clear inductive structure; 5-6 = external model provides substantially complete inductive proof where SxS winner has none', 'rating': 6}, {'name': 'Explicit handling of directionality in proof', 'description': "GPT 5.2 clearly labels and separates the (⇒) and (⇐) directions with explicit headers and proof strategies, while the SxS winner uses informal directional markers ('From bit-vectors to integers' / 'From integers to bit-vectors') without explicit logical structure.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = external model has minor organizational improvement; 3-4 = external model has clear directional separation; 5-6 = external model has substantially clearer logical structure', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Construction details for model building', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 provides explicit numbered steps (1-4) for constructing the T_ufia interpretation in the (⇐) direction, including standard integers, parameter interpretation, variable interpretation, and recursive function definitions, while the SxS winner gives a compressed construction without step-by-step detail.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = external model has minor additional detail; 3-4 = external model has clear construction steps; 5-6 = external model has substantially more explicit and verifiable construction', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'Explicit justification of restriction relevance', 'description': "GPT 5.2 includes a dedicated subsection explaining why 'no extract' and 'no concrete constants' restrictions matter, with technical justification about width-changing operations and additional translation clauses, while the SxS winner only mentions this in a parenthetical final sentence.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = external model has minor additional explanation; 3-4 = external model has clear technical justification; 5-6 = external model has substantially more thorough explanation of restrictions', 'rating': 5}, {'name': 'LaTeX formatting for formal notation', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 uses proper LaTeX display math environments (\\[...\\]) for formal definitions and multi-line equations with alignment, while the SxS winner uses inline math and simple align* without consistent structural formatting for definitions.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = external model has minor formatting improvement; 3-4 = external model has noticeably better LaTeX structure; 5-6 = external model has substantially superior formal notation presentation', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit termination justification for recursion', 'description': "GPT 5.2 explicitly states and justifies termination for the recursive definitions in Lemma 2 ('Each recursive axiom application replaces k by k-1...the recursion is well-founded'), while the SxS winner does not mention termination at all.", 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = external model mentions termination briefly; 3-4 = external model provides clear termination argument; 5-6 = external model provides substantially more rigorous termination justification', 'rating': 5}], 'sxs_winner_label': 'Response A', 'token_usage': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 44465, 'output_tokens': 4369, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.141358}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.141358}, 'token_usage_cumulative': {'gemini': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'openai': {'input_tokens': 0, 'output_tokens': 0, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.0}, 'kimi': {'input_tokens': 44465, 'output_tokens': 4369, 'cached_tokens': 0, 'cost_usd': 0.141358}, 'total_cost_usd': 0.141358}}] 
