ess'); buzzwords ('rigorous', 'precise', 'superior command'); no quoted excerpts from responses; perfect recall of specific LaTeX artifacts; diplomatic structure with concession clause; generic evaluative language without personal voice."}, 'rubric_fields': [{'rubric_index': 1, 'name': {'result': 'pass', 'issue': ''}, 'description': {'result': 'fail', 'issue': "Uses formal academic register with precise but generic phrasing ('explicitly states', 'including which direction(s)'); lacks concrete, actionable criteria; reads like LLM-generated formal specification."}}, {'rubric_index': 2, 'name': {'result': 'pass', 'issue': ''}, 'description': {'result': 'fail', 'issue': "Similarly formal and abstract ('clearly indicates', 'explicitly verifies', 'required properties'); templated parallel structure with first rubric; no specific examples of what 'verification' looks like."}}]}}, 'justification_grammar_check': {'status': {'result': 'fail', 'issue': "American English spellings detected: 'behavior' should be 'behaviour', 'center' should be 'centre', 'organize' should be 'organise', 'analyze' should be 'analyse', 'realize' should be 'realise'. Also contains em dash '—' which is disallowed."}, 'severity': 2, 'flagged_fields': {'ab_comment': {'result': 'pass', 'issue': ''}, 'human_ab_gpt_comment': {'result': 'fail', 'issue': "Contains em dash '—' in 'unnecessary pedantry—the recursion'. American English: 'behavior' should be 'behaviour'."}, 'human_ab_gemini_comment': {'result': 'fail', 'issue': "American English: 'behavior' should be 'behaviour', 'center' should be 'centre' in 'centered'."}, 'rubric_fields': [{'rubric_index': 1, 'description': {'result': 'pass', 'issue': ''}}, {'rubric_index': 2, 'description': {'result': 'pass', 'issue': ''}}]}}}, 'rubric_comment_grounding': {'status': {'result': 'fail', 'issue': 'Critical failures: ab_preference is 0 (tie) but ab_comment clearly states B is better. Rubric ratings are inconsistent with comparison comments. GPT and Gemini ratings appear swapped or unjustified given comment content.'}, 'severity': 1, 'rubrics': [{'rubric_index': 1, 'name_grounded': {'result': True, 'issue': ''}, 'description_grounded': {'result': False, 'issue': "Rubric description is generic and not specifically grounded in either comparison comment. Neither comment explicitly discusses 'which direction(s) of the if-and-only-if will be proved' as a distinct evaluative criterion. The Gemini comment criticizes GPT's proof structure labeling, not explicit strategy statement. The GPT comment praises unified construction but doesn't frame it as 'explicit proof strategy statement'."}, 'gpt_rating_consistent': {'result': False, 'issue': "gpt_rating is 6 (substantially better) but human_ab_gpt_comment states GPT 5.2 is 'excessively verbose with redundant structure' and 'belabors the obvious' while praising Gemini (SxS winner). The comment clearly favors Gemini over GPT, so GPT should have low rating (1-2), not 6. Rating contradicts comment sentiment."}, 'gemini_rating_consistent': {'result': False, 'issue': 'No gemini_rating provided for this rubric (only human_gpt_rubric fields populated), cannot validate consistency.'}}, {'rubric_index': 2, 'name_grounded': {'result': True, 'issue': ''}, 'description_grounded': {'result': False, 'issue': "Rubric description mentions 'each direction' and 'interpretation construction', but human_ab_gemini_comment actually criticizes Gemini for misstating proof structure and having 'garbled LaTeX artifacts', not for failing to indicate interpretation construction. The comment focuses on errors, not this specific criterion. Description not well-grounded in actual comment content."}, 'gpt_rating_consistent': {'result': False, 'issue': 'No gpt_rating provided for this rubric (only human_gemini_rubric fields populated).'}, 'gemini_rating_consistent': {'result': False, 'issue': "gemini_rating is 4 (noticeably better) but human_ab_gemini_comment heavily criticizes Gemini with 'critical errors', 'garbled