uality criteria. Neither rubric name appears in or relates to the actual comparison comment content. The rubric descriptions describe what models 'should' do rather than concrete evaluable features. Ratings of 5-6 are unjustified given comments don't mention these specific criteria."}, 'severity': 1, 'rubrics': [{'rubric_index': 1, 'name_grounded': {'result': False, 'issue': "Rubric name 'Binomial Coefficient Properties Stated' is vague and generic - describes a procedural step, not a concrete quality. Not mentioned in either comparison comment. Name describes what the response should contain, not a specific evaluable feature."}, 'description_grounded': {'result': False, 'issue': "Description 'Response explicitly states which properties... will be relied upon' is procedural checklist language, not concrete criteria. Neither comment mentions whether binomial coefficient properties were stated upfront. Description is not grounded in actual comment content."}, 'gpt_rating_consistent': {'result': False, 'issue': "Rating of 6 (substantially better, SxS winner clearly lacks) is unjustified. Comment praises GPT's 'elegant, unified proof' but never mentions whether binomial coefficient properties were stated upfront. No evidence in comment supports this specific rating."}, 'gemini_rating_consistent': {'result': False, 'issue': 'No gemini_rating provided for this rubric, but the rubric structure is malformed (only one rubric per model instead of shared rubrics with separate ratings).'}}, {'rubric_index': 2, 'name_grounded': {'result': False, 'issue': "Rubric name 'Lucas's Theorem Relevance Identified' is vague and procedural. Not mentioned in either comparison comment. Describes what should be identified rather than a concrete quality feature."}, 'description_grounded': {'result': False, 'issue': "Description 'identifies where Lucas's theorem... becomes relevant' is procedural. human_ab_gemini_comment mentions Lucas's theorem in passing but doesn't evaluate whether Gemini 'i