2026-03-25 10:47:39,473 494048 INFO ? odoo.addons.preference_ranking.models.models: eval_oph response: [{'task_id': 'tv_stem_5796', 'prompt': 'You are given a setup and statement to prove or derive. Your job is to provide a complete and correct proof. Think carefully, trying multiple approaches if you are stuck, and finally give a cleaned up proof under the heading ## Proof. If you are unable to complete the proof, be honest and say so.\n\n## Setup\nThe theory under consideration is Maxwell-dilaton-massive gravity in four dimensional space-time, described by the action:\n$$\nI=\\frac{1}{16 \\pi} \\int d^{4} x \\sqrt{-g}\n\\left(\\mathcal {R}-F_{\\mu\\nu} F^{\\mu\\nu} -2(\\nabla \\varphi)^2-V(\\varphi)\n+ e^{-2\\beta \\varphi}\\mathcal {L}_m\\right),\n$$\nwhere $\\mathcal{R}$ is the Ricci scalar, $F_{\\mu\\nu}$ is the electromagnetic field tensor, $\\varphi$ is the dilaton field with potential $V(\\varphi)$, and $\\beta$ is a coupling constant. The last term denotes the nonminimal coupling of the scalar dilaton field to the massive graviton. $\\mathcal {L}_m$ is the graviton action given by:\n$$\n\\mathcal {L}_m= m_0^2 \\sum_{i=1}^{4} \\eta_i \\mathcal {U}_i(g,h)\n$$\nwhere $m_0$ is the mass of the graviton, and $\\eta_i$ are dimensionless parameters. $h$ is a fixed rank-2 symmetric tensor, and $\\mathcal{U}_i$ are polynomials of the matrix $K^{\\mu}_{\\nu}=\\sqrt{g^{\\mu\\tau}h_{\\tau\\nu}}$ satisfying the following recursion relations:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\mathcal{U}_1 &= [K] \\\\\n\\mathcal{U}_2 &= [K]^2 - [K^2] \\\\\n\\mathcal{U}_3 &= [K]^3 - 3[K][K^2] + 2[K^3] \\\\\n\\mathcal{U}_4 &= [K]^4 - 6[K]^2[K^2] + 8[K][K^3] + 3[K^2]^2 - 6[K^4]\n\\end{align*}\nwhere $[K] = K^\\mu_\\mu$.\n\nThe equations of motion obtained by varying the action with respect to the field variables $g_{\\mu\\nu}$, $\\varphi$ and $A_{\\mu}$ are:\n\\begin{align*}\nG_{\\mu\\nu} = \\mathcal{R}_{\\mu\\nu}-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathcal {R} g_{\\mu\\nu} &= 2\\partial_{\\mu}\\varphi\\partial_{\\nu}\\varphi -