t spaces by showing kernel preservation in both directions and surjectivity via the reduction identity (*). For Prompt Correctness, both properly interpret the graded polynomial identity framework and (FT)*-action. For Writing Style, both use clear sectioning with similar logical flow—SxS winner uses 'Strategy' and numbered sections 1-5, while GPT 5.2 uses 'Strategy (outline)' and numbered sections 1-6. For Verbosity, both are comparably detailed; GPT 5.2 explicitly constructs the reduction operator ρ_n with a formal claim/proof structure, while SxS winner integrates this more compactly into surjectivity. Neither contains errors or omissions warranting preference; the singleton case treatment is essentially identical in both."}, 'rubrics_vs_gemini': [], 'rubrics_vs_gpt': [{'name': 'Explicit homomorphism construction', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly constructs an algebra homomorphism ξ: F⟨X^{T-gr}⟩ → F⟨X|H⟩ on generators before restricting to multilinear spaces, whereas the SxS winner only defines a linear map on the multilinear subspace without establishing the underlying algebraic structure.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = marginally better, 3-4 = noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 = substantially better with clear deficiency in SxS winner', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Bidirectional identity preservation proof', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 provides explicit bidirectional proof (⇒ and ⇐) that f ∈ Id^{T-gr}(A) ⟺ ξ(f) ∈ Id^H(A) with clear substitution constructions, while the SxS winner conflates this reasoning across injectivity and surjectivity sections without standalone clarity.', 'scale': '1-6 scale: 1-2 = marginally better, 3-4 = noticeably better with clear evidence, 5-6 = substantially better with clear deficiency in SxS winner', 'rating': 4}, {'name': 'Explicit reduction operator definition', 'description': 'GPT 5.2 explicitly defines the linear reduction operator ρ_n on basis monomials with a precise formula involving products h_1(t_1)⋯h_n(t_n), whereas the